Hydra patches for gpui_ce_wgpu 0.3.0 (crates.io), for the Linux build.
Applied on 2026-11-15 to the vendored copy in vendor/gpui-ce-wgpu (then
under rewrite/; the registry crate copied byte for byte, then from the
repository root:

    git apply --recount --directory=vendor/gpui-ce-wgpu vendor/gpui-ce-wgpu.hydra.patch

`--recount`: the hunk headers' line counts were written by hand; run from
the crate's own folder, git apply skips every path without a word). Kept as
the record of the change; vendor/gpui-ce/HYDRA-PATCHES.md ("gpui_ce_wgpu
0.3.0") lists it and the later edits. ../gpui-ce/src/window.rs's
`with_element_mask_group` and `with_element_transform_group` now fall back
only on macOS (`cfg!(target_os = "macos")`: the Metal renderer is still
crates.io's). What it does:

- An isolated content-filter group composites through its boundary's mask
  fade (mask groups, `BlurUniforms::with_edge_fade`) and its transform
  (transform groups, `BlurUniforms::with_transform`), as
  ../gpui-ce-windows/src/directx_renderer.rs `dx_blur_and_composite` does.
  `BlurUniforms` keeps its 112 bytes (the assert in filters.rs holds).
- Backdrop filters and every other caller keep `blur_and_composite`
  unchanged (no extras).

Written against the 0.3.0 sources on Windows; first built in WSL on
2026-11-15 (see the shell notes in docs/parity-big-picture.md).

